
PDC EXPERIMENT 2 - PARALLEL SEARCH AND SORT
Environment: Ubuntu Linux + GCC + OpenMP

===============================
PART A: PARALLEL LINEAR SEARCH
===============================

1. Open terminal:
   Ctrl + Alt + T

2. Create file:
   nano search.c

3. Paste the Parallel Linear Search C code.
   Save: Ctrl + O, Enter
   Exit: Ctrl + X

4. Compile:
   gcc -fopenmp search.c -o search

5. Execute:
   ./search

6. Expected output:
   Found at index 6


========================================
PART B: ODD-EVEN TRANSPOSITION SORT
========================================

1. Create file:
   nano sort.c

2. Paste the Odd-Even Sort C code.
   Save: Ctrl + O, Enter
   Exit: Ctrl + X

3. Compile:
   gcc -fopenmp sort.c -o sort

4. Execute:
   ./sort

5. Expected output:
   Sorted Array:
   10 20 30 40 50 60 70 80


===============================
IMPORTANT COMMANDS AND KEYWORDS
===============================

Check compiler:
gcc --version

Compile with OpenMP:
gcc -fopenmp filename.c -o program

Run program:
./program

Set requested threads in code:
omp_set_num_threads(4);

Parallel loop:
#pragma omp parallel for

Search synchronization:
#pragma omp critical

SEARCH MEMORY ORDER:
Array -> Key -> Found -> Threads
-> Parallel loop -> Compare -> Critical -> Print

SORT MEMORY ORDER:
Array -> Phases -> Even/Odd
-> Compare -> Swap -> Repeat -> Print
